{
  "case_id": "2019-18-935",
  "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:10 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "SOPAN JOSHI, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting neither party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Amir C. Tayrani)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Hague Convention on the Civil Aspects of Child Abduction is designed to protect children who have a country of habitual residence from the harmful effects of wrongful removal from that country. In this case, however, the Convention was applied to separate two-year-old A.M.T. from her mother, the only caregiver A.M.T. had ever known, and to return the child to Italy, a country where A.M.T. had spent only the first eight weeks of her life."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: -- Tayrani, a -- a problem with your position, I take it your view is this child, taken to the United States at eight weeks old, has no habitual residence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Amir C. Tayrani)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Hague Convention sets a goal of resolving these cases within six weeks. This case has been going on for four and a half years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So assuming, as I do, that there has to be something that can secure greater rights for her, why should it be here instead of there, assuming -- and you don't want me to assume this -- that the totality of the circumstances suggests that she has acclimated?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Tayrani",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. TAYRANI: Well, first of all, because Italy was not A.M.T.'s country of habitual residence. So she never should have been returned to Italy in the first place. The only way to remedy that wrong --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. TAYRANI: She is four and a half"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Hague Convention is designed to protect children who have a stable -- stable, settled existence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Tayrani",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. TAYRANI: The Convention would not apply if a child had no country of habitual residence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: How -- how long does the child have to -- how old does a child have to be before you would say they have a habitual residence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "district court found, at Pet. App. 94a, that Monasky intended to return to the United States with A.M.T. as soon as possible."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry, where did you get that standard? I look at the European court and it had a different standard. It says some degree of integration by the child in a social and family environment. That's the definition the Bates Court, Lady Hale, adopted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner counsel",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As Justice Ginsburg pointed out, it would largely eliminate the Convention's protection for very large -- for very young children because they would have no habitual residence and because one of the spouses in the cases where there is marital discord during the pregnancy and the birth could simply say I withhold agreement on where the child should live, and that would mean there was no habitual residence as long as there was no agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner counsel",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner cites some cases saying that a child may not have a habitual residence, but I think it's important to point out that those statements were made in a very different context, which is actually the one presented in the very large majority of decided Convention cases, and that's the situation where the child and the parents live together in country A, then the child moves to country B with one or both parents -- it could be a temporary stay with grandparents, could be for a job -- and then the parent who was with the child in country B says, I'm not sending the child back."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Which -- which, as you say, is what Judge Boggs said. And so I'm curious as to why you're not just accepting that as a formulation of the legal standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Wouldn't all the work be done on \"absent unusual circumstances,\" though? And so you would still have the out, as Justice Kagan points out, for people to argue that it's --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
      "evidence_id": "ev-655cb3d39600-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, what this \"take everything into account and be flexible\" standard seems to mean in practice -- and you tell me if this is wrong -- is there are a lot of different considerations and they may -- particular considerations may be more important in one case than in another case, so we're just going to dump this in the hands of a particular judge to make a decision that that particular judge thinks is fair in accordance with that particular judge's value judgments, and we're not going to make it -- we're going to make it very hard to get that reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-18-935",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "655cb3d39600e0fca56dd6469194182d25b3ccbe7770a7e0cb20d69ed8003d86",
